cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the article
  that introduced the method.
title: "RECpy: particularized demand forecasting and day-ahead scheduling for energy communities"
abstract: >-
  RECpy forecasts next-day electricity demand for each consumer in an energy
  community and schedules a shared battery against day-ahead prices. Each
  consumer is given its own forecasting model, selected from fifteen
  machine-learning regressors, ARIMA and SARIMAX, and three deep-learning
  architectures by a Wilcoxon signed-rank tournament with multiple-comparison
  control. The selected forecasts drive a linear programme solved with Pyomo and
  HiGHS. Every setting lives in a configuration file, so adapting the framework
  to another community requires no code changes.
type: software
